# wasm-shell — the home screen's links ("bookmarks").
#
#   name | source (file path or http/https URL) | description
#
# The source is exactly what the CLI accepts, so anything listed here can also
# be opened with `cargo run -p host -- <name>`. Remote entries are the point:
# a mini-app is fetched and sandboxed at runtime, with no host rebuild.

counter    | mini-apps/counter/counter.component.wasm       | A counter; the count lives inside the guest.
hello      | mini-apps/hello/hello.component.wasm            | A second app, to show hot-swap with no host rebuild.
counter-cs | mini-apps/counter-cs/counter-cs.component.wasm  | The counter written in C# (.NET NativeAOT) — same WIT, no host change.
